00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.280
It turns out

345
00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.440
the memory bound case is really hard because the matrices are really small.

346
00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:48.480
So there are two kernels or two types of kernels we really care about.

347
00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.840
Context is when you do your pre-filled.

348
00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:52.480
So this is before you've got your cave cache.

349
00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:56.400
And when you generate your KB cash for this, I, I will

